{
  "name": "Speed to Lead: reply to HubSpot form leads in seconds with Claude, Gmail and Slack",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "cfc151d9-e1cd-4829-89fc-920a2dce95c2",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -128,
        -32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 1040,
        "content": "## Speed to Lead: reply to HubSpot form leads in seconds with Claude, Gmail and Slack\n\n### How it works\n\n1. A new HubSpot form submission creates a contact and fires a webhook; CSV imports and list syncs are filtered out.\n2. The workflow fetches the contact, verifies a real form submission exists, and applies an optional form allowlist.\n3. Claude drafts a short personal reply from the lead's actual message plus your business context.\n4. The draft is posted to Slack with Send it / Don't send buttons. Nothing is emailed without approval; unapproved drafts auto-decline after 24 hours.\n5. On approval, Gmail sends the reply with your signature, the touch is logged on the HubSpot contact timeline, and Slack gets a confirmation.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Create a HubSpot private app with contact read and write scopes; connect its token here and add a contact.creation webhook subscription pointing at this workflow's production URL.\n- [ ] Add Anthropic credentials for the Claude drafting node.\n- [ ] Connect Gmail OAuth credentials (the signature request also needs the Gmail settings read scope).\n- [ ] Connect a Slack bot with chat:write and invite it to your channel.\n- [ ] Fill in Configure Reply Settings: company name, sender name, what you do, booking link, and optionally allowedForms (comma separated; empty means every form).\n\n### Customization\n\nTone, length and call to action live in Configure Reply Settings, no prompt editing needed. Adjust the approval button labels, or remove the approval step if you fully trust the drafts. Swap Gmail for your own email node if you send from elsewhere."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "838305c0-6b60-4e2b-a510-8afbe4c7c241",
